---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BrandMark from '../components/BrandMark.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About">
<section class="page-hero about-hero"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span></span> Workshop profile</div><h1>A workshop with a memory.</h1><p>Redwind Workshop is a personal engineering record: a place for ongoing builds, experiments, failures, field notes, and the ideas connecting them.</p></div><span class="about-seal"><BrandMark size={126}/></span></section>
<section class="content-section manifesto"><blockquote>Build things. Learn in public. Keep the failures. Leave enough of a trail that the next version of you can understand what happened.</blockquote><div class="manifesto-grid"><section><h2>Why it exists</h2><p>Most project sites show only finished work. This one treats the process itself as worth preserving: revisions, wrong turns, test results, repairs, and small discoveries included.</p></section><section><h2>What belongs here</h2><p>Embedded systems, radio, robotics, software, mechanical projects, fabrication, space, and anything else interesting enough to deserve a notebook.</p></section><section><h2>The visual language</h2><p>Industrial solarpunk rather than corporate futurism: durable tools, repairable systems, field-ready hardware, technical drawings, natural forms, and technology imagined as something compatible with a good future.</p></section></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
